//@version=6
// MORAI · Vol State — the two questions a calendar seller asks, plotted over time.
//
// A calendar sells the front and owns the back. Two things decide whether that is worth
// putting on, and neither of them is a price level:
//   · VRP  — is implied above realized? Below 1.0 you are PAYING to sell volatility.
//   · TERM — is the curve in contango? Flattening means the front is bid, the condition
//            MORAI's own entry gate penalises and then blocks.
// Both are computed HERE, live, from series TradingView already carries. Nothing is pushed
// in from MORAI, so nothing can go stale.
//
// RATIOS, NOT VOL POINTS — the LEVEL of vol lies across a regime change; the ratio does not.
// Predicting Alpha argue the same against IV rank: "Typical metrics such as IV rank and
// percentile won't work, since they rely on the historical data." Their SPX figure,
// IV ~ 1.3 x RV, is the 1.3 line. Both series being ratios centred on 1.0 also means they
// share ONE axis. Never a second scale.
//
// TIMEFRAME LAW: every request names "D" explicitly (a daily series requested at
// timeframe.period returns na on ANY intraday chart), and every derived statistic is
// computed INSIDE its request.security() call so it evaluates on DAILY bars. Computing
// ta.stdev() outside would run it over chart bars, which on a 30m chart repeat the same
// daily value ~13 times — measuring copies of one number against itself.
//
// lookahead_on is REQUIRED and safe here: with lookahead_off, request.security() returns the
// last COMPLETED daily bar, so on Friday evening it hands back THURSDAY's close (verified:
// 17.09 against a real Friday close of 15.99). This drives no backtest.
//
// It DOES now drive the alertconditions at the foot of this file, so the trade-off is worth
// stating plainly: with lookahead_on the daily values are today's forming bar, which is what
// you want on a live chart and NOT what you want in a backtest. The consequence is that an
// alert can fire mid-session and the condition can un-fire before the close if VIX reverses.
// Treat a fired alert as "go look", never as a completed daily signal.
indicator("MORAI · Vol State", overlay = false, precision = 3)

// ─── Inputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// MUST be a plain input, never a computed expression. request.security() requires a SIMPLE
// string for its symbol. An earlier version used
//     string undSym = und == "" ? syminfo.tickerid : und
// to fall back to the chart symbol; the ternary demotes the result to SERIES string and the
// study then dies with a bare "cannot compile script" only when added to a chart — the Pine
// editor reports zero errors, so it surfaces as an empty pane with a red marker and nothing
// else. Default matches how SPX actually resolves on this layout: SPCFD:SPX, not SP:SPX.
string und = input.symbol("SPCFD:SPX", "Underlying for realized vol",
     tooltip = "VIX is the 30-day implied vol OF SPX, so realized must come from SPX too.")
int  rvLen = input.int(20, "Realized vol lookback (daily bars)", minval = 5)
int  pctLb = input.int(252, "VIX percentile lookback (daily bars)", minval = 60)
bool showGate = input.bool(true, "Tint background with the entry gate")
bool tlShow = input.bool(true, "Show traffic-light panel")
int  termLb = input.int(5, "Term-slope lookback (daily bars)", minval = 1,
     tooltip = "How far back to measure whether the curve is flattening. Daily bars, not " +
               "chart bars — see the TIMEFRAME LAW note at the top.")

// ─── Fetch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
d(string sym) =>
    request.security(sym, "D", close, ignore_invalid_symbol = true,
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

float vix   = d("CBOE:VIX")
float vix3m = d("CBOE:VIX3M")

// Annualised realized vol in vol points, evaluated on daily bars. 252 is the trading-day
// convention — worth knowing the Predicting Alpha corpus never states an annualisation
// convention anywhere across all 59 articles, so this is a choice, not a quote. It only has
// to be consistent; the ratio is unitless either way.
float rv = request.security(und, "D",
     ta.stdev(math.log(close / close[1]), rvLen) * math.sqrt(252) * 100,
     ignore_invalid_symbol = true, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

float vixPct = request.security("CBOE:VIX", "D", ta.percentrank(close, pctLb),
     ignore_invalid_symbol = true, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// The daily close termLb DAILY bars ago. `term[termLb]` would be wrong: on a 30m chart that
// is termLb chart bars (2.5 hours at the default), not termLb sessions — the same trap the
// TIMEFRAME LAW note describes. The shift has to happen inside request.security().
dBack(string sym, int n) =>
    request.security(sym, "D", close[n], ignore_invalid_symbol = true,
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

safeDiv(float a, float b) => na(a) or na(b) or b == 0 ? na : a / b

float vrp  = safeDiv(vix, rv)      // > 1.0  -> implied above realized -> you are paid
float term = safeDiv(vix3m, vix)   // > 1.0  -> contango -> front cheap vs back

float termPrev = safeDiv(dBack("CBOE:VIX3M", termLb), dBack("CBOE:VIX", termLb))

// ─── Entry gate ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Mirrors MORAI's entry-gate.ts, inverted for this pane. entry-gate.ts holds VIX/VIX3M with
// penalty at .90 and block at .95; this series is VIX3M/VIX, so those become 1/.90 = 1.111
// and 1/.95 = 1.053 — same rule, reciprocal. VIX 20/25 is MORAI's ladder. The percentile arm
// is Predicting Alpha's: "if there were going to be a time where you risk blowing up, this
// would be it."
float TERM_PENALTY = 1.111, TERM_BLOCK = 1.053
bool blocked = (not na(vix) and vix >= 25) or (not na(term) and term <= TERM_BLOCK)
bool penalty = not blocked and ((not na(vix) and vix >= 20)
     or (not na(term) and term <= TERM_PENALTY)
     or (not na(vixPct) and vixPct >= 80))

// ─── Verdicts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two of them, because opening and holding are not the same question.
//
// NEW is the stricter one, on purpose. Putting a calendar ON demands both engines be paid:
// contango (the leg you own is the richer one) AND a positive VRP (the front you are selling
// is priced above what the index is actually delivering). Miss either and there is no reason
// to pay the debit today rather than next week.
//
// HELD is looser, and deliberately ignores the VIX-percentile arm of the gate. A high
// percentile is an entry-TIMING concern; a vol spike is not automatically bad for a position
// that is already long vega. What actually damages a calendar you hold is the curve
// flattening — your short front gaining on your long back — which is the term arm, and
// realized outrunning implied, which is VRP. Those two, nothing else.
//
// This panel cannot see your P&L. Pine has no position data. "TAKE PROFIT" means the reason
// you put the trade on is going away — if you are green, that is the cue. If you are red it
// is a judgement call no chart can make for you.
//
// A dead data feed must never read as a green light, so every verdict is gated on haveData
// first. Both `blocked` and `penalty` are built from `not na(...)` guards and go FALSE when
// the series are missing, which without this would render as "ENTER" on an empty pane.
bool haveData = not na(vix) and not na(term) and not na(vrp)
bool vrpOk    = not na(vrp) and vrp >= 1.0
bool termFall = not na(term) and not na(termPrev) and term < termPrev
bool holdRisk = (not na(term) and term <= TERM_PENALTY) or not vrpOk

string entryTxt = not haveData ? "NO DATA"
     : blocked ? "DO NOT ENTER"
     : (penalty or not vrpOk) ? "WAIT" : "ENTER"

string heldTxt = not haveData ? "NO DATA"
     : blocked ? "CLOSE NOW"
     : holdRisk ? "TAKE PROFIT"
     : termFall ? "WATCH" : "HOLD"

// ─── Plots ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Blue/amber is the canonical CVD-safe pair, and each line also carries its own right-edge
// label, so identity never rests on hue alone.
color VRP_C = #2e86de, TERM_C = #e67e22
color GO = #26a69a, WARN = #f0b429, STOP = #ef5350, MUTED = #5c6879

color entryCol = not haveData ? MUTED : blocked ? STOP : (penalty or not vrpOk) ? WARN : GO
color heldCol  = not haveData ? MUTED : blocked ? STOP : holdRisk ? WARN : termFall ? WARN : GO

plot(vrp,  "VRP · VIX/RV",     color = VRP_C,  linewidth = 2)
plot(term, "Term · VIX3M/VIX", color = TERM_C, linewidth = 2)

// 1.0 means the same thing for both series: below it you are selling vol for less than it is
// realizing, or the curve has inverted.
hline(1.0, "Parity", color = #5c6879, linestyle = hline.style_solid)
hline(1.3, "SPX normal VRP", color = #3a4453, linestyle = hline.style_dotted)

bgcolor(showGate ? (blocked ? color.new(#ef5350, 88)
     : penalty ? color.new(#f0b429, 91) : na) : na, title = "Entry gate")

// ─── Right-edge readout ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The two value labels ride ON their lines, so they stay useful when the panel is off.
var label lV = na, var label lT = na

if barstate.islast
    label.delete(lV)
    label.delete(lT)
    lV := label.new(bar_index + 3, vrp, na(vrp) ? "VRP —" : "VRP " + str.tostring(vrp, "#.##"),
         style = label.style_label_left, color = #0f1521, textcolor = VRP_C, size = size.small)
    lT := label.new(bar_index + 3, term, na(term) ? "TERM —" : "TERM " + str.tostring(term, "#.##"),
         style = label.style_label_left, color = #0f1521, textcolor = TERM_C, size = size.small)

// ─── Traffic-light panel ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Position is fixed rather than an input: the pane has one sensible corner for this, and one
// less setting is one less way to get it wrong. Toggle it off if it covers the lines.
// Every row carries a WORD as well as a colour — the verdict never rests on hue alone.
var table tl = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 5, border_width = 0,
     frame_width = 1, frame_color = #27313f)

if barstate.islast
    if tlShow
        table.cell(tl, 0, 0, "NEW", text_color = #9aa3b8, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tl, 1, 0, entryTxt, text_color = entryCol, text_size = size.normal)

        table.cell(tl, 0, 1, "HELD", text_color = #9aa3b8, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tl, 1, 1, heldTxt, text_color = heldCol, text_size = size.normal)

        // Below the verdicts, the three numbers they were computed from. A verdict you
        // cannot audit from the same panel is a black box.
        string vrpWord = na(vrp) ? "—" : vrp >= 1.3 ? "rich" : vrp >= 1.0 ? "paid" : "PAYING"
        table.cell(tl, 0, 2, "VRP", text_color = #9aa3b8, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tl, 1, 2, na(vrp) ? "—"
             : str.tostring(vrp, "#.##") + "  " + vrpWord,
             text_color = vrpOk ? #d6dbe4 : WARN, text_size = size.small)

        string termWord = na(term) ? "—"
             : term > TERM_PENALTY ? "contango"
             : term > TERM_BLOCK ? "flattening" : "INVERTING"
        string termArrow = na(termPrev) ? "" : termFall ? " ▼" : term > termPrev ? " ▲" : " ="
        table.cell(tl, 0, 3, "TERM", text_color = #9aa3b8, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tl, 1, 3, na(term) ? "—"
             : str.tostring(term, "#.##") + termArrow + "  " + termWord,
             text_color = na(term) ? MUTED : term > TERM_PENALTY ? #d6dbe4 : WARN,
             text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(tl, 0, 4, "VIX", text_color = #9aa3b8, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tl, 1, 4, na(vix) ? "—"
             : str.tostring(vix, "#.#") +
               (na(vixPct) ? "" : "  " + str.tostring(vixPct, "#") + "%ile"),
             text_color = #d6dbe4, text_size = size.small)
    else
        table.clear(tl, 0, 0, 1, 4)

// ─── Alerts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Fire on the TRANSITION, not the state — a level-triggered alert on "blocked" would fire
// every bar for as long as the condition holds.
alertcondition(blocked and not blocked[1], "Vol State · gate BLOCKED",
     "Calendar gate blocked — VIX >= 25 or term at/below 1.053. Close on strength.")
alertcondition(penalty and not penalty[1], "Vol State · gate PENALTY",
     "Calendar gate degraded — take profit on open calendars if green.")
alertcondition(not blocked and not penalty and (blocked[1] or penalty[1]),
     "Vol State · gate OPEN", "Calendar gate clear again.")
